  institution = {MH370 Flight Path Reconstruction Group},
  note = {UNPUBLISHED and NOT PUBLICLY AVAILABLE. No date, report number or locator is given by the only source that cites it. This is reference [8] of Holland (2018). SCOPE, read exactly off Holland's text: [8] tested ``a number of different SDUs'' for the effect of power outages on the BFO at power-on, and found -- from Inmarsat BFO logs for 9M-MRO covering FOUR log-ons after SATCOM outages in the week before the accident flight -- that this satellite data unit gives a BFO initially too high at log-on followed by a simple decay to steady state. The seven-log-on set in Holland's own table and figures, which includes the accident flight's 18:25:27Z log-on as log-on 7, is Holland's extended compilation and is NOT attributed by him to [8]. So [8] is the origin of the oven-controlled crystal oscillator start-up decay MODEL and of the four-log-on evidence for it; the seven-log-on calibration is Holland's. It can only be cited as ``cited in Holland (2018)''. Flagged for the adversarial review: the bench-test evidence underlying the 00:19 transient model is not in the public literature.},
}

